BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Asheville 20s-40s Social Group
UID:event_316474716@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260926T045026Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261005T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261005T220000
SUMMARY:Game Night @ Archetype West Asheville
DESCRIPTION:Asheville 20s-40s Social Group\n\\*\\*This is a collaboration 
 with the Asheville's Bored Game Geeks\\*\\*\n\nBring your favorite game(s)
  or learn a new one – members are always happy to teach! See you there a
 nd have a blast!\n**Welcome to the Game Night Extravaganza!**\n\nCalling a
 ll dice-rollers\, card-shufflers\, and strategy-curious adventurers!\nAre 
 weeknights feeling a tad mundane? Fear not! We’ve got the antidote: **Bo
 ard Games\, Brews\, and Bliss**.\n\n**Our Mission:** To ignite laughter\, 
 forge alliances\, and maybe—just maybe—unleash a few friendly rivalrie
 s & battle to the death!\nNo PhD in rulebooks required! Whether you’re a
  Settlers of Catan enthusiast or a Code Names solving ninja\, or your firs
 t time touching a board game ***we will explain all the rules needed.***\n
 \nExpect:\n\n* **Beer on Tap**: Because rolling dice is better with a pint
  in hand.\n* **Low Brainpower Required**: We’re all about fun\, not Ferm
 at’s Last Theorem.\n* **Epic Showdowns**: Ticket to Ride routes\, Splend
 or gem heists\, and High stakes Camel Up.\n\nFeel free to request any game
  you’d like to play or bring your own. So gather your guild\, stack your
  resource cards\, and let the games begin! May your laughter be loud\, you
 r moves be bold\, and your victory dances be legendary.\n\nSee you at the 
 table!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-20s-40s-social-group/events
 /316474716/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260908T205604Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260908T205604Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Asheville 20s-40s Social Group
UID:event_316701927@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260926T045026Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T220000
SUMMARY:A Night of Swing Dancing - Beginners Welcome!
DESCRIPTION:Asheville 20s-40s Social Group\nWant to try something a little
  different on a Friday night?\n\nCome learn to swing dance at Asheville Sw
 ing Night! Swing dancing has its roots in the jazz and swing era of the 19
 20s–40s\, and there's something pretty fun about learning the same dance
 s people were doing nearly a century ago.\n\nIt's upbeat\, social\, and pl
 ayful\, with plenty of partner changes\, spins\, and opportunities to meet
  new people.\n\nAnd you absolutely do **not** need to know what you're doi
 ng before you arrive!\n\nThe night starts at 7PM with a beginner lesson de
 signed for people who are brand new to swing dancing. You'll learn the bas
 ic footwork and a few moves to get you out on the dance floor.\n\nMost peo
 ple rotate partners during the lesson\, so there's no need to bring one\, 
 and plenty of people come alone.\n\nThen at 8PM\, the lesson wraps up and 
 the DJ takes over for two hours of social dancing. 🎶\n\n**What dance ar
 e we learning?**\nEast Coast Swing\, a style of swing dancing that grew ou
 t of the swing era of the 1920s–40s and is still danced all over the wor
 ld today.\n\n**I've never danced before. Is that okay?**\nAbsolutely. The 
 7PM lesson is specifically designed for beginners. Just be sure to arrive 
 on time\, the lesson builds progressively\, so it's difficult to jump in l
 ate if you're brand new.\n\n**How many people will be there?**\nUsually ar
 ound 50–70 people attend throughout the evening. Asheville Swing Night i
 s open to the public\, so it's much bigger than just our Meetup group.\n\n
 **Do I need a partner?**\nNope! Most people rotate partners during both th
 e lesson and social dance\, and coming alone is completely normal.\n\n**Wh
 at should I wear?**\nWhatever you're comfortable moving in. You'll see eve
 rything from jeans and T-shirts to vintage-inspired outfits. Comfortable s
 neakers or leather-soled shoes work well\; heels aren't recommended.\n\n**
 Does our Meetup group hang out together all night?**\nNot exactly. We'll m
 eet up before the lesson\, but once it begins\, we join everyone else and 
 rotate partners. During the social dance\, some Meetup attendees may hang 
 out together and chat\, while others (including the hosts) will be out dan
 cing and mingling around the room.\n\nSo think of this less as a Meetup wh
 ere our group sits together all evening and more as a chance to experience
  Asheville's swing-dance scene together.\n\n**LOGISTICS**\n\n📍 Haw Cree
 k Commons\nParking is onsite\, with overflow parking at Haw Creek Elementa
 ry. Just walk across the field to the venue.\n\n🚪 Doors open at 6:45PM\
 n\n🕖 **7PM sharp** — Beginner swing dance lesson\n\n💃🕺 **8–10
 PM** — Social dancing with DJ\n\n💵 **$10** — includes the lesson + 
 dance\nCash or Venmo at the door\n\n**More Info:**\nFacebook event: [https
 ://www.facebook.com/events/1668229217573197/](https://www.facebook.com/eve
 nts/1668229217573197/)\n\nWebsite: [https://ashevilleswingnight.com/](http
 s://ashevilleswingnight.com/)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-20s-40s-social-group/events
 /316701927/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260924T235729Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260924T235729Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
